6. Data layer
Inputs per review
SOW (required).
Contract and proposal (supporting; the proposal enables scope-drift detection).
Optional free-text notes from the delivery manager.
Reference data
Internal policy (legal and general). Converted into structured rules: topic, standard
position, acceptable fallback, severity weight, owner. Target 20 to 40 rules for the first
version.
Lessons library (past contracts and delivery issues). Each entry: clause pattern,
what went wrong, impact (cost, delay, dispute), how it could have been caught. Start
with 10 to 20 curated entries.
Storage
Hackathon: files and a local vector index; reports stored as JSON plus an exported
document.
Later: a document store with access control, audit log of each review, and versioning
of policy rules.
Data handling
Contracts are sensitive. Remove client names for demo data, keep processing within
approved environments, and log what was sent to the model.
7. Evaluation
Test set
5 to 10 SOWs and contracts (real with names removed, or synthetic) with planted
risks: vague scope, buried uncapped indemnity, conflicting payment terms, missing
assumption, unrealistic resourcing.
An answer key listing each known issue, its clause, and its expected severity.
Metrics
Recall: share of known issues the agent finds (primary metric).
Precision: share of reported findings that are real and useful (false-positive rate).
