3. Is the output advisory only, or does it feed an approval workflow or gate?
Data and access 4. Can we get 5 to 10 real or anonymised SOWs and contracts, and who
approves their use? 5. Is the internal policy documented in a usable form, and who owns it
and can validate our rule extraction? 6. Is there a record of past contract-driven delivery
issues, and in what form (tickets, post-mortems, dispute logs)? 7. Do we have access to
historical pricing and effort data to sanity-check resource numbers?
Risk and governance 8. Are we allowed to send contract text to an external model API, or
must it stay in an approved environment? Are there client confidentiality restrictions? 9.
Where is the line between what a delivery manager can decide and what must go to legal?
Can we define the escalation thresholds? 10. How should the risk score be used:
informational, or tied to approval limits?
People and validation 11. Can a legal reviewer and a delivery manager give us time to
validate findings and the severity ranking? 12. Who owns the tool after the hackathon, and
who is the first pilot user group? 13. What are the judging criteria and demo format, so we
can design the demo around them?
